Hello all, here are the plans for the family reunion, and who's bringing what.

My sister is expecting her second child in the spring. We are all delighted, =
and her eldest has already announced that he would like a brother, please.

I took up watercolours again after many years. My first few attempts were mud=
dy, but the evening class has helped, and I am quite pleased with a painting =
of the harbour.

The weather has finally turned. We lit the fire for the first time this seaso=
n last night, and the cat has claimed the rug in front of it as her own.

Thank you again for the recipe. I made the soup on Sunday and everyone went b=
ack for seconds, even my brother, who usually refuses anything with lentils i=
n it.

It was good to hear your news on the phone. I am glad the new job is going we=
ll, and that the journey is shorter than you expected once you found the righ=
t train.

We drove up to the lakes for a day last week. The leaves were just starting t=
o change, and we had a picnic by the water before the clouds came in.

The village fete is next Saturday. There will be the usual cake stall and dog=
 show, and I have somehow been talked into helping with the tombola.

We went to the farmers' market on Saturday and came home with far too much ch=
eese. The bread stall was excellent too, and the man there remembered us from=
 last time.

The dog has been enjoying the cooler mornings. We have started walking the lo=
ng way round the lake, and she always stops to say hello to the ducks by the =
old boathouse.

The apple tree has given us a huge crop this year. We have made crumble, chut=
ney and juice, and there are still boxes of apples in the garage waiting for =
a plan.

The kittens next door have discovered our garden. They chase leaves across th=
e lawn every afternoon, and I confess I spend far too long watching them from=
 the window.

We are looking forward to seeing you at the end of the month. The spare bed i=
s made up, and I have found the board game we used to play, so be ready for a=
 rematch.

Could you bring the folding chairs and arrive by eleven on the Saturday?

--=20
Mia

